# Agent Guidance: {{projectName}}

This project was scaffolded by `@nakedev/nest-scaffold` (`{{cliVersion}}`) and is
maintained using its `generate` subcommands — new modules, services,
controllers, and {{#if isMicroservice}}RPC methods{{else}}endpoints{{/if}} are
not hand-written.

## Hard rule: use the CLI to add new modules/services/controllers/methods

If you are about to write a **new** NestJS module, service, controller,
{{#if isMicroservice}}gRPC handler,{{else}}route handler,{{/if}} or add a
**new** {{#if isMicroservice}}RPC method{{else}}endpoint{{/if}} to an existing
one — stop and run the CLI instead:

```bash
npx nest-scaffold generate module <name> --full
npx nest-scaffold generate method <module> <methodName> --type <get|post|put|patch|delete>
```

This applies **even when the request doesn't say "module" or "method" or name
the CLI at all**. Recognize indirect asks as generation work, for example:

- "add a way to reset a user's password" → a new `post` method on the
  relevant module (`generate method users resetPassword --type post`)
- "let admins approve orders" → a new method on the orders module
  (`generate method orders approve --type patch`)
- "we need an endpoint that lists overdue invoices" → a new `get` method
  (`generate method invoices findOverdue --type get --get-mode all`)
- "add a products feature" → a whole new module
  (`generate module products --full`)

Run `npx nest-scaffold generate --help` (or `g me --help`, `g m --help`) to see
all flags before hand-writing anything that looks like scaffolding.

## What the CLI does NOT do — these are still done by hand, as normal

- Business logic inside a generated stub (the CLI leaves `TODO`-style bodies —
  filling them in is your job)
- Entity field changes (adding/removing/renaming columns, relations)
- DTO validation rules (`@IsEmail()`, `@Min()`, etc. beyond the generated
  skeleton)
- Bug fixes, refactors, or edits to existing logic
- Anything in a project that does **not** have `nest-scaffold.config.json` at
  its root — that means the project wasn't scaffolded by this CLI, and this
  rule does not apply

## Command quick reference

{{#if isMicroservice}}
- `npx nest-scaffold generate module <name> --full` — layered module
  (`domain/`, `application/`, `infrastructure/`) with entity, gRPC controller,
  service, and a registered `.proto` file
- `npx nest-scaffold generate method <module> <name> --type <get|post|put|patch|delete>` —
  adds one RPC to an existing module's controller + service + `.proto`
{{else}}
- `npx nest-scaffold generate module <name> --full` — controller + service +
  DTOs + entity, registered in `AppModule`
- `npx nest-scaffold generate method <module> <name> --type <get|post|put|patch|delete>` —
  adds one route to an existing module's controller + service
{{/if}}
- `npx nest-scaffold generate service <name>` / `generate controller <name>` —
  add a missing half of a module
